<title>CHINA: Tjiwi Kimia sets US$600 mln 144a bond.</title>
<headline>Tjiwi Kimia sets US$600 mln 144a bond.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tjiwi Kimia Finance Mauritius has priced a US$600 million 144a bond guaranteed by PT Pabrik Kertas Tjiwi Kimia Tbk, said lead manager and bookrunner Goldman Sachs.</p>
<p>The senior unsecured bond matures in August 2004 and is non-callable for life. It carries a coupon of 10 percent and was re-offered at 99.455 to yield 10.11 percent or 400 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>The bond is rated Ba3 by Moody's Investors Service and BB by Standard and Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The bond was expected to be US$400 million in size.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852)2843-6371</p>
</text>
